Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:16:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] r6_fit: the clothing's printed outline on the silhouette
 is body of unknown colour, not floor

The Roblox template prints a near-black border round each side; where a side
faces the camera at the silhouette (a leg seen from the side) that border is the
body's outermost ~0.15 stud and was classified floor. outline_of marks dark
pixels (v <= 40) that hug a body patch, lie in a thin part of the dark (gone under
an opening scaled by the patch's half-thickness) and within a band of it, as
UNKNOWN. Wide dark areas (a black shirt of another avatar, dark floor) stay floor.
Enabled per palette ('outline' in side_colours.json). Measured on idle frames with
the tracked params: left 518 .867 -> .925, right 292 .909 -> .923, back 102
.947 -> .949, front 792 unchanged. Not built (python tool only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HQYiYmhRzcQpLCYMVVDQeZ
